ables de la planificación y supervisión de la nutrición de los pacientes, asegurando que sus necesidades dietéticas sean atendidas de manera efectiva y personalizada.\",3\r\n57,ALIMENTACIÓN,\"\"\"Alimentación\"\" encompasses a broad range of dietary management strategies and practices essential for maintaining health and nutritional status across various patient populations. It refers to the act of eating, which is closely linked to swallowing processes that can be impacted by conditions such as dysphagia. In the context of healthcare, alimentación involves dietary aspects and nutritional care provided to patients during hospitalization, ensuring that their dietary intake is adequate, whether it is normal or deteriorated.\n\nFor patients with specific health conditions, such as pancreatitis or head and neck cancers, alimentación plays a critical role in alleviating symptoms and providing necessary nutritional support. It also includes the assessment of eating habits through tools like the Mini Nutritional Assessment, which evaluates nutritional intake and overall health.\n\nFurthermore, alimentación addresses the feeding practices and nutritional strategies vital for the health and growth of infants, particularly those who are preterm. It emphasizes the importance of hydration and nutrient intake, which are crucial for maintaining physical performance and overall well-being.\n\nIn summary, alimentación is a multifaceted concept that involves the careful planning, preparation, and provision of food and hydration tailored to meet the needs of individuals, particularly those facing health challenges, ensuring their safety and promoting optimal health outcomes.\",12\r\n11723,DIETA CONTROLADA EN HIERRO,\"A controlled iron diet is a dietary regimen designed to manage iron levels in patients with conditions like hemochromatosis, focusing on reducing iron intake.\",4\r\n7906,CONSUMO ALIMENTARIO,\"Consumo alimentario refers to the act of consuming food, which is linked to health and the preparation of meals at home.\",3\r\n\n\n-----Relationships-----\nhuman_readable_id,source,target,description,combined_degree\r\n663,NUTRICIÓN,PACIENTE,\"The entity \"\"PACIENTE\"\" is currently receiving nutritional attention due to a state of malnutrition. This patient is undergoing nutritional assessments and interventions specifically designed to improve their health, particularly in the context of severe malnutrition. Nutritional support is deemed essential for this patient, especially given their risk of malnutrition, which is critical for recovery from any underlying health issues, including eating disorders. Adequate nutrition through specialized diets is necessary to restore the patient's body weight and enhance overall health. Thus, the focus on \"\"NUTRICIÓN\"\" is vital for the patient's recovery and well-being.\",755\r\n679,NUTRICIÓN,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,\"NUTRICIÓN encompasses the broader process of providing essential nutrients to individuals, which includes various methods of nutritional support. One specific method within this framework is NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL, which serves as an alternative approach when enteral nutrition is insufficient or not feasible. NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL is particularly important for patients who are unable to consume food orally, ensuring they receive the necessary nutrients for their health and recovery. This method highlights the critical role of NUTRICIÓN in patient care, as it provides a vital nutritional intervention when traditional enteral feeding methods cannot be utilized. Overall, NUTRICIÓN and NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL work together to ensure that patients receive adequate nutritional support tailored to their specific needs.\",647\r\n3493,PACIENTE,DIETISTAS,Los dietistas trabajan con el paciente para optimizar su ingesta dietética durante la nutrición enteral.,549\r\n683,NUTRICIÓN,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,\"NUTRICIÓN and NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL are interconnected concepts within the field of nutritional support. NUTRICI